{"author":{"id":"e0b5a45ee94df92761e1991b03f72f45cac91cde564e2faac1223bf52a3fe292"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1788139158,"nonce":"8uVj9NG+kMOVuolkvNKuL0qQVjA=","target":"9d35d147234d354f9f6031edf019eacddf663d3024c195bff508c1fd5f222f9f","message":"DISCLOSURE + ACCESSOR FINDINGS — 2.4 worker, branch `spec/2.4-world-serializers`,\nsix commits, `dotnet build -c Release` clean at every one of them. No DLL\ncommitted; the game was never launched.\n\n(Reposted: `git-bug bug comment new -F` silently DROPS every line beginning with\n`#`, so the first version of this comment lost all of its markdown headings.\nNo heading here starts with `#`.)\n\n**Undeclared addition: the `world-fixture` dev verb**\n\nDeclared here as `pawn-fixture` and `journal-selftest`'s steps were. New file\n`Source/AutoRimmer/WorldFixtureVerbs.cs`, gated on `Prefs.DevMode`, one `dev`\njournal event per step with the established `{verb, step, target}` payload,\nsuperseded by 3.1.\n\nSteps: `bench` `bill` `stockpiles` `growing` `research` `letter` `open-letter`\n`forbid` `fire`. Every one publishes an `expect_*` block computed independently\nof the serializers — two readers, one truth.\n\nIT USES TWO OF THE THREE GOD-HAND CALLS DESIGN'S ACTION MODEL NAMES, AND SAYS SO\nIN THE FILE. `BillStack.AddBill` checks nothing (not `AvailableNow`, not the\n15-bill cap) and `ResearchManager.SetCurrentProject` tests only `baseCost \u003e 0f`.\nThe fixture is dev-layer so it may; it picks a runnable recipe and a\nprerequisite-met project itself so the resulting state is legal; and a wave-3\nPLAYER verb may not take either shortcut. `open-letter` calls\n`Letter.OpenLetter()`, which stacks a force-pausing dialog — clear it with\n`journal-selftest {\"steps\":[\"dialogs-clear\"]}` before advancing.\n\n**Two hazards in SHIPPED files, for the orchestrator to route**\n\nNeither is mine to fix (new-files-only), and neither blocks this spec.\n\n1. `Spatial.cs` (2.3, merged) TRIPS A LAZY SCRIBED WRITE ON EVERY `map-view`.\n   `CropRenderer.Cell` calls `zg.GetPlantDefToGrow()` to build the zone legend.\n   `Zone_Growing.PlantDefToGrow`'s getter does\n   `if (plantDefToGrow == null) plantDefToGrow = \u003cToxipotato or Potato\u003e` after\n   running `PollutionUtility.SettableEntirelyPolluted`, and `plantDefToGrow` is\n   `Scribe_Defs.Look(...)`. So `map-view` over a never-configured growing zone\n   PINS its plant forever — including pinning potato on a zone that would later\n   have defaulted to toxipotato. 2.4's `zones` reads the backing field instead\n   and reports `plant_configured:false`; `map-view` should use\n   `WorldSafe.PlantToGrow(zg)` and label the legend \"growing: unconfigured\" when\n   it is null. One line, someone else's file.\n\n2. `Zone.Cells` ADVANCES THE SHARED `Rand` STREAM, and nothing on main uses it —\n   keep it that way. The getter runs `cells.Shuffle()` on first access, which is\n   Fisher-Yates over `Rand.RangeInclusive` (`Verse/GenList.cs`), and\n   `cellsShuffled` re-arms on every `AddCell`/`RemoveCell`. It also permanently\n   reorders a `Scribe_Collections` list. This is `_mp/DETERMINISM.md`'s\n   \"`Rand.*` in UI/draw code\" class in observer clothing, and it is reached from\n   `Zone_Growing.ContentsStatistics`, `GetInspectString` and\n   `IPlantToGrowSettable.Cells` — i.e. from every obvious way to answer \"what is\n   growing here\". `WorldSafe.ZoneCells()` is the route; `Zone.CellCount` and\n   `AllSlotCellsList()` are safe.\n\n**The three save-writing accessors this spec had to route around**\n\nRecorded because they will bite 3.x too, and because in each case the WRITE is\ninvisible at the call site.\n\n- `ResearchManager.GetProgress` INSERTS ON A MISS (`progress.Add(proj, 0f)`, and\n  `anomalyKnowledge.Add` for a knowledge project). Both dictionaries are\n  scribed. `ResearchProjectDef.ProgressReal` is that call; `IsFinished` is\n  `ProgressReal \u003e= Cost`; `PrerequisitesCompleted` is `IsFinished` over the\n  prerequisites; `CanStartNow` is all of them; AND `RecipeDef.AvailableNow`\n  reaches it too. So `AllDefs.Where(p =\u003e p.CanStartNow)` — the obvious research\n  serializer — would add one zero entry per research project on the bench (six\n  DLCs plus mods) to the save on the first call, permanently.\n  `WorldSafe.Progress/Finished/PrereqsDone/CanStart` re-derive the whole ladder\n  from the backing dictionaries; `GetTechprints` right beside it is a plain\n  `TryGetValue` and is safe.\n- `Bill_Production.ShouldDoNow` WRITES THE SCRIBED `paused` on three paths, and\n  `Bill.BaseColor` calls it, which is why the bill list looks like a read.\n  `WorldSafe.BillState` gives the same answer from the stored fields;\n  `paused_stored` publishes the flag as saved.\n- `ResearchManager.CurrentAnomalyKnowledgeProjects` INITIALISES AND ADDS TO A\n  SCRIBED LIST ON READ (`EnsureKnowledgeProjectsInitialized`), and\n  `GetProject(category)` / `IsCurrentProject` both route through it.\n  `GetProject()` with a null category returns `currentProj` directly and is\n  safe. Anomaly knowledge projects are therefore not enumerated, and `research`\n  says so in a `note` field rather than silently omitting them.\n\n**Doc changes I could not make (file rule) — recommend for the orchestrator**\n\n- JOURNAL.md: the `dev` row lists `journal-selftest` and `pawn-fixture` as the\n  writers of that type; `world-fixture` joins them.\n- README.md's git-bug trap list: `-F` also drops every line beginning with `#`,\n  at STORAGE, not only in `show`. Both of this session's comments lost their\n  headings to it before being reposted. The list names `-F` for apostrophes and\n  `show` for headings; the real rule is that a `-F` body must not start a line\n  with `#` at all.\n- DESIGN.md decisions log: worth an entry that the observer surface has its own\n  gate-in-the-widget rule — where the game's own accessor writes, the serializer\n  re-implements the derivation and cites the member. Four now do.\n- DESIGN.md, Observation model, would be the right home for the standing fact\n  that `Alert_FireInHomeArea` is the ONLY vanilla fire alert and is scoped to\n  the home area, so the alert readout is structurally blind to a fire on\n  unclaimed ground. `things.fire` and the `fires` verb close it, but the digest\n  (2.1's file, not mine) still cannot see one — I WOULD FILE THAT AS ITS OWN\n  ISSUE: a `fires` count belongs in the digest's threat section, and it is four\n  lines in `DigestVerb.ThreatSection`.","files":null}]}